  "verdict": "holds",
  "detail": "At 98d7781b5 runStage3 ran replay.py with stage3_skip_stages=[beard_shadow], so detail_bands ran on the SOCKET output; runBeardSubStage then wrote albedo_beard.png from albedo_socket.png as the stage final. The detail product was discarded and the manifest order beard_shadow(7) -> detail_bands(8) was not honoured; chain.ts executedChainStages listed even the skipped stages and finalName preferred albedo_socket.png.",
  "evidence": "packages/openclinxr/factory-stations/src/face_realism/the-station-runs-every-manifest-stage.test.ts G1/G1c/G1d failed at 98d7781b5, green after the fix"
 },
 "fix": {
  "approach": "replay skips beard_shadow + detail_bands; the station chains their standalone runners in manifest position; executed list and final derive from manifest output_paths (planChainManifest)",
  "reason": "replay.py's beard branch passes --vermilion-mask (handback 8), the standalone runner does not, so letting replay run beard would change its bytes vs the pins and the wrinkle lineage; standalone detail reuses replay's mask construction (vermilion via replay._vermilion_union, eye/brow unions bitwise OR as replay builds them inline)",
  "orderingGuard": "segmented execution: consecutive replay-run stages go through replay.py as one invocation; a replay-run stage after a station-chained stage runs in a further invocation with --albedo set to the previous segment final and every other stage skipped (derive never name-skipped: it seeds via --skip-ao + existing derive_out, replay.py:116; name-skipping it would refuse at replay.py:87)"
 },
